  "finding": "No selected App-language value living only in a custom SwiftUI environment override or separate application setting was found in the inspected standalone and combined entry/settings chains. This is a bounded source conclusion, not proof that Foundation locale, bundle localization and SwiftUI locale always agree at runtime.",
  "priorAudit": {
    "commit": "770bc4e4a38ec299a8f0ebcc3cc5e8f0c170dabc",
    "path": "docs/validation/20261127-wave2-native-root-error-language/source-manifest.original.json",
    "sourceCount": 27,
    "scope": "Reuse exact prior paths and whole-source hash identities; no resource-catalog audit repeated."
  },
  "observedSourceFlow": [
    {
      "route": "Standalone",
      "flow": [
        "NativeApp/Sources/AnyNativeApp.swift: WindowGroup",
        "AnyNativeRootView(application:)",
        "AnyUIErrorText.text"
      ],
      "languageOwner": "No selected-language state, Apple-language defaults write, or .environment(\\.locale, ...) exists in this entry/root. The DEBUG fixture overlays do not supply locale."
    },
    {
      "route": "Combined Any",
      "flow": [
        "AppScene.AnytypeApp.WindowGroup",
        "PinkhaEngineSceneView.engineContent",
        "PinkhaEmbeddedAnyRootView",
        "AnyNativeRootView(session:)"
      ],
      "languageOwner": "Engine selection persists only pinkha.app.selected-engine.v1. No inspected wrapper assigns locale; AnyView preserves the supplied subtree rather than creating a language preference."
    },
    {
      "route": "Combined Heart",
      "flow": [
        "AppScene",
        "ApplicationCoordinatorView.setupGlobalEnv",
        "TorahEditorHostModifier @Environment(\\.locale)",
        "session.updateEffectiveLocale(locale)"
      ],
      "languageOwner": "The host forwards the inherited environment on document load and locale.identifier change. Session initializes effectiveLocale to Locale.autoupdatingCurrent, then uses the forwarded locale for Torah messages/association labels; this is consumption, not a user-selected override."
    },
    {
      "route": "Existing settings",
      "flow": [
        "SettingsView/SettingsViewModel",
        "SettingsAppearanceView/SettingsAppearanceViewModel"
      ],
      "languageOwner": "The inspected controls/model cover profile, account, appearance, icon and other existing actions; no separate App-language property, persisted choice or locale environment modifier is present."
    },
    {
      "route": "Bilingual AnyUI helper",
      "flow": [
        "AnyDocumentPresentation.swift: AnyUIErrorText.text"
      ],
      "languageOwner": "Locale.autoupdatingCurrent.language.languageCode?.identifier == \"he\" selects Hebrew, otherwise English. No argument or SwiftUI Environment locale is accepted."
    },
    {
      "route": "Original Loc",
      "flow": [
        "Loc.tr",
        "BundleToken.bundle.localizedString",
        "String(format: locale: Locale.current, arguments:)"
      ],
      "languageOwner": "Bundle.module under SWIFT_PACKAGE, otherwise Bundle(for:). Locale.current supplies formatting, not an explicitly selected localization bundle. No private language bundle override is introduced here."
    },
    {
      "route": "Actual queued Native UI selection",
      "flow": [
        "NativeLaunchTests.makeApplication",
        "XCUIApplication.launchArguments",
        "NativeApplicationUnderTest.launch→super.launch"
      ],
      "languageOwner": "Hebrew uses -AppleLanguages (he,en) plus -AppleLocale he_IL; English RTL/styled path replaces both with (en,he) and en_US. The unified wrapper subsequently operates the real engine selector and does not rewrite these arguments."
    }
  ],
  "relevantDistinctions": [
    "Heart's explicit effectiveLocale consumer and AnyUIErrorText's Foundation consumer use different APIs. The inspected production chain does not create a conflicting locale value, so differing APIs alone do not establish a bug.",
    "No claim is made that Locale.autoupdatingCurrent is OS-only, App-only, or equal to the SwiftUI environment or bundle preference on all supported Apple systems.",
    "The recovery phrase's explicit layoutDirection.leftToRight subtree is a content-direction exception, not a language-selection owner.",
    "The existing Native UI tests request language/locale at process launch. Their source does not establish actual opposite-OS runtime behavior.",
    "AppConfigurator's registry and AppDelegate/SceneDelegate entry bodies were read for the concrete startup chain; this audit does not claim a repository-wide semantic review of all configurator implementations."
  ],
